// Package gen holds the iikoCloud types and operation table generated by
// tools/gen/cloud from https://api-ru.iiko.services/api-docs/docs. types.go and
// operations.go are generated; this file is not.
//
// # What the generator does not carry over
//
// The list is exact rather than reassuring: each entry is a place where the
// spec says more than these types do, and a caller has to know which.
//
//  1. Polymorphism. Go has no sum type, so a field whose schema is one of the
//     14 discriminated bases is json.RawMessage — 82 fields, 48 of them slices.
//     The concrete variants (SimpleOrganizationInfo, CashPayment,
//     ProductOrderItem, …) are ordinary structs that embed their base, so a
//     request field is json.Marshal(gen.CashPayment{…}) and a response field is
//     json.Unmarshal(raw, &v) after reading the discriminator property.
//  2. oneOf with more than one member (2 places) is json.RawMessage. A oneOf of
//     a single member is flattened to that member.
//  3. nullable is ignored, on all 921 properties that carry it. Optional fields
//     are value types with omitempty, so an explicit null cannot be sent, and a
//     field that arrived as null is indistinguishable from one that was absent.
//     Pointers on 840 structs would be worse; make a field a pointer by hand if
//     an operation is ever shown to need the difference.
//  4. Inline object schemas inside a property are json.RawMessage. The
//     generator does not invent a name for an anonymous type.
//  5. Enums are named only at the top level: 53 types with constants. The 14
//     inline enums on properties stay plain string, so their values are not
//     constrained. Integer enums become int with constants named after the
//     number (ProgramType0), because the spec carries no member names.
//  6. Validation is dropped: maxLength, minLength, pattern, minimum, maximum
//     and maxItems appear on 48 properties and emit nothing. So does default,
//     which in this spec is a string even on booleans.
//  7. format only chooses int32 versus int64. uuid and date-time stay string on
//     purpose: iikoCloud stamps are "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.fff", and decoding
//     those into time.Time fails silently.
//  8. Operation parameters are not modelled. All 306 carry exactly one — the
//     Timeout header, default 15 s — which rest.Config.Timeout sets by hand.
//  9. additionalProperties:{} becomes map[string]json.RawMessage.
//  10. The 8 x-webhooks entries are not operations. Their payload schemas exist
//     as types, but nothing here receives or dispatches a webhook; the webhooks
//     domain only manages the subscription.
//
// Deprecated operations (22) are not generated. Deprecated schemas are: the
// spec does not mark them, and guessing by name would drop live types.
package gen
